WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.690
- [Narrator] Europe hasn't had a hurricane

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.390
reach its shore in over 50 years.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.970
Now don't get the wrong idea.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.980
Hurricane season still brings
a hefty dose of wind and rain.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.330
But Europe has something
that North America doesn't,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.723
when it comes to protection
against hurricanes.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:16.755
Location.

00:00:16.755 --> 00:00:19.255
(light music)

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.930
Hurricanes usually form off
the coast of West Africa,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.790
where warm water near the
Equator and high humidity

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.560
create columns of rapidly
rising rotating air.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.380
It's the perfect recipe for a storm.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.860
Now the more warm, moist air
that the system picks up,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.980
the stronger it becomes.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.150
That's why a tropical
storms can quickly grow

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.521
into a full on hurricane as it
marches across the Atlantic.

00:00:45.521 --> 00:00:46.690
(soft music)

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.420
Now normally hurricanes are propelled

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.630
on a westward track by the trade winds,

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.040
caused by the Earth's rotation.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.070
That's why Europe as well
as the West Coast of the US,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.110
rarely experience full on hurricanes.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.010
But that's not the whole story.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.377
After all, since the year 2000,

00:01:02.377 --> 00:01:06.230
remnants of around 30
hurricanes have reached Europe.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:10.030
For comparison, Florida
has seen 79 real hurricanes

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.403
over the same time frame.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.310
By the time these remnants make landfall,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.200
they've went from a hurricane force,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.000
to a tropical storm or weaker.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.930
And that's where Europe's
location comes into play.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.310
In order for a hurricane
to head towards Europe,

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.810
something crucial has to happen.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:31.810
It has to travel really far
North by about 200 miles.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.940
Once a storm system
reaches 30 degrees north,

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:38.210
it encounters the subtropical jet stream.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.120
Which moves in the opposite
direction of the trade winds.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.060
And therefore, blows the storm East

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.650
But because the storm
is now farther North,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.240
the waters underneath are colder

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.700
by up to about five to 10 degrees Celsius.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.360
Which means less energy
available to feed the storm.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.780
And as a result, it starts
to die down by the time

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.930
it's headed for Europe.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.290
Even though it's no longer a hurricane,

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.300
it still packs a punch when it hits shore.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.200
In fact, most of these hurricane remnants

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.260
will combine with other nearby
cyclones and weather fronts,

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.810
that create high winds and rain

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.580
that mainly hit Ireland and Great Britain.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.160
But have been known to
reach as far as Greece

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.573
or even farther in Northern Russia.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.310
Typical damages include power outages,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.670
flooding, and occasionally casualties.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:30.350
Most recently the remnants
of Hurricane Ophelia

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.330
made landfall in Ireland
and Scotland in 2017.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:38.690
About 50,000 households in
Northern Ireland lost power.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.750
Three deaths were reported
and downed trees closed many

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.120
of the public roads and highways.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.890
This was the worst storm that
Ireland had seen in 50 years.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.630
And it may be a sign of what's to come.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.880
As global surface temperatures rise,

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.490
it will also increase the
sea surface temperatures

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.240
in the Northern Atlantic.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.390
Which researchers estimate
could contribute to an increase

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:05.030
in the number of hurricane
force storms that reach Europe.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.230
Some experts predict that by
the end of the 21st century,

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.383
Europe could experience, on average,

00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:14.630
13 powerful storms each year
during hurricane season.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.183
Compared to the two per year it sees now.

